-# Single owner native Avalanche driver
-
-`AvalancheDriver` borrows the runtime and dispatcher, which must outlive it.
-It owns quorum, poll engine, bounded peer adapter, and public peer file. Supply
-an explicit private session key; it is never printed or persisted. An absent
-`local_proof.proof` selects a nonvoting observer. Restart with an explicit native
-proof and matching signed delegation after funding; no key or stake is invented.
-The supplied chain/genesis/validation digest must match the runtime.
-
-Call Start with explicit IBD state and Unix seconds, then Tick with explicit
-IBD, monotonic milliseconds, and Unix seconds. Drain dispatcher notices: call
-Activate for Activated, Handle for Avalanche Application, and Disconnect for
-Closed. Demultiplex mixed transaction/proof inv and getdata into proof-only
-Application notices before Handle. Retain a notice on Backpressure. Retry
-Activate on Backpressure (including Hello enqueue pressure). Tick retains the
-same allocated OutgoingPoll on peer Backpressure and pumps outbound actions;
-never allocate a replacement poll to retry that enqueue. All methods and runtime
-mutations run on one owner with no callback reentry. Discovery is tick-driven, with a bounded per-connection requester deadline of at
-least60seconds. Successful responses re-anchor that deadline after remote request
-processing; backpressure preserves the pending retry.
-Call Reconcile for authoritative blocks/proofs the node elects to reconcile.
-No HTTP or index publication is performed here.
-
-Runtime snapshots require authoritative idle storage, authenticate up to eleven
-indexed ancestors for median time, and fence tip/context generation/revision.
-Real tip/context changes revalidate all quorum proofs before application input,
-or polling. Persistence saves the last active admitted public records even when
-runtime recovery is pending; it makes no current eligibility claim. Start
-revalidates each restored record against the recovered chain. Pollable proofs automatically enter polling at admission, restoration, and
-revalidation; initial acceptance comes from the current quorum vote. Existing
-records retain their accumulated vote confidence. Obsolete proof records are
-pruned before enrollment, including after replacement. If live block/proof records
-fill the configured capacity, admission remains valid, existing polls continue,
-and Tick reports Backpressure while retrying pending proof enrollment. Each block
-status maps by name to the runtime enum.
-The runtime still atomically checks every update tip/generation. Restore screens
-records against actual native coins, skips stale records individually, then uses
-Quorum's validated atomic restore to retain registered metadata. Store framing,
-foreign-profile, and durability failures return a typed PeerStoreCode; save
-failure revokes driver readiness. Public envelopes are bounded by quorum storage
-and pruned when displaced, invalidated, or stale.
-
-Voting policy equals pinned ABC defaults: stake dust 100 COIN, 2016 confirmations,
-minimum quorum stake 1e12 base units, default connected ratio and eight proof
-inventory peers. Bootstrap must mine native Payment outputs, obtain 2016
-confirmations, aggregate sufficient stake, and connect enough independently
-provisioned authenticated peers. The dev monetary profile's small original
-funding fixtures do not satisfy those amounts. This driver does not modify them,
-reduce thresholds, or claim observer startup establishes a quorum. Operator
-provisioning must build native-bound signed proofs and signed session delegations,
-then pass the private session key separately from public proof/delegation files.
-
-Standalone checks use actual Session/Transport/Dispatcher handshake, actual
-DevelopmentRuntime genesis/header storage, signed absent-coin proof envelopes,
-and actual atomic PeerStore files in fresh private temporary directories. They
-cover observer lifecycle, native profile fencing, explicit IBD/monotonic inputs,
-strict maturity policy, repeated completed discovery/requester cooldown and
-expiry, stale restored proof screening, typed storage failure,
-and rejection of a configured proof whose coin does not exist. They do not
-claim a mature funded quorum, successful finalization, or live networking.
-
-```
-cmake -S src/lotus_v2/avalanche_driver_test -B /private/tmp/lotus-v2-ava-driver-build -G Ninja \
-  -DLOTUS_ABC_BUILD=/path/to/pinned/build \
-  -DLOTUS_SECP_LIBRARY=/path/to/pinned/build/src/secp256k1/libsecp256k1.a \
-  -DLOTUS_BOOST_INCLUDE=/path/to/boost/include
-cmake --build /private/tmp/lotus-v2-ava-driver-build --target avalanche_driver_test
-ctest --test-dir /private/tmp/lotus-v2-ava-driver-build -R ^avalanche_driver_test$ --output-on-failure
-```
-
-Driver Tick reports `DriverResult::disconnected_peer` after removing a terminal
-peer's adapter actions, discovery state, authentication and poll query ownership.
-The transport owner must close that connection; the development node does so
-before processing the rest of Tick's result. Missing/closed discovery and poll
-targets terminate only that peer. Busy output and action pressure remain
-retryable. A live dispatcher CapacityRefused remains ProtocolFailure, preserving
-local configuration/invariant failures rather than concealing them as disconnects.
-A retained application for a dead peer returns UnknownPeer before runtime proof
-refresh or application callbacks. The focused driver test queues an actual
-response, removes the dispatcher connection before Pump, and verifies terminal
-cleanup is reported while the driver stays ready and no discovery retry remains.
-
-The response callback propagates PollReceiveResult explicitly. The peer consumes
-Ignored authenticated late replies without closing the connection. Rejected
-remote content remains a peer failure; failed local chain snapshot or commit
-remains LocalFailure. The legacy bool PollEngine::Receive predicate returns true
-only for Applied; callers requiring peer disposition must use ReceiveResponse.
-
-Passive diagnostics expose separate protocol layers. Poll counters track query
-creation, expiry/cancellation and matched/applied/ignored/rejected/local-failure
-responses. `live_queries` and `live_records` are current gauges. Before counters
-saturate, created queries equal matched plus expired plus cancelled plus live
-queries. Peer outcome counters cover response handler results; its fixed
-rejection categories cover every rejected application, including responses, so
-these two views overlap deliberately. Ignored engine responses may become peer
-rejections at the existing abuse threshold; they are never labelled applied.
-
-Driver `poll_actions_queued` counts adapter queue acceptance, not socket writes;
-`poll_backpressure` counts attempts, including retries. Disconnect totals count
-tracked Avalanche connections once, with exactly one explicit cause category.
-Endpoint owners pass the actual transport cause when available; otherwise the
-Unknown category is used. Duplicate close notifications do not add a second
-count or rewrite the first cause. Unknown is never inferred by subtraction.
-All counters saturate at UINT64_MAX and are never consulted by voting, ownership,
-cooldown, eligibility or scheduling decisions. Reading Status/Diagnostics never
-expires queries, generates polls, changes confidence, revalidates proofs or
-establishes quorum. Optional tip confidence is absent when the current authority
-is unavailable or no live tip record exists; runtime tip_finalized identifies a
-finalized absence. No keys, proof IDs, hashes or retained query traces are added.
