-// Copyright (c) 2026 The Lotus developers
-#ifndef LOTUS_V2_DEVELOPMENT_NODE_COMMAND_H
-#define LOTUS_V2_DEVELOPMENT_NODE_COMMAND_H
-namespace lotus::v2 {
-// Linux/macOS isolated single-owner development process only:
-// lotusd -lotusv2node MANIFEST DATADIR NETWORK.json
-// NETWORK is exact
-// schema1:{schema,magic,listen:{address,port},connect:[{address,
-// port}],receive_limit,local_policy:"bounded-local-v1"}. Addresses numeric;
-// listen port0 is explicit OS allocation. No endpoints/magic/seeds/profile
-// defaults. Manifest supplies all consensus profiles and max body bytes
-// (<=receive_limit).
-//
-// Selected local policy is operational, NOT consensus: <=8 connections/targets,
-// 65536 decoded txs/body, 4096 candidates, 64MiB resident bodies, 128MiB
-// journal, 16MiB undo/body and 64MiB aggregate preparation bodies/undo, fork
-// depth16; downloads <=8 jobs, 128MiB/peer and256MiB global staging;
-// independent serving leases <=96MiB globally; transport output
-// <=receive_limit+4096 bytes/peer. Slot/byte quotas exclude
-// allocator/container/kernel/LevelDB overhead (not RSS). Each loop bounds
-// accept/connect/notices/queries/I/O and sleeps via poll<=10ms. Connect
-// retry1s, header refresh1s plus authoritative-tip notification, handshake 10s,
-// request10s/lifecycle60s. JSON stdin one line<=2*bodycap+4*65536+1024,
-// Optional network avalanche:{credentials:null|absolute_path,
-// initial_download:{minimum_height:u32,maximum_tip_age_seconds:positive_u32}}.
-// Absent disables Avalanche; null credentials creates an ephemeral observer
-// session. Credentials is an owned private regular nonsymlink file <=1MiB,
-// exact {schema:1,session_key:32-byte lowerhex,proof:V2 proof-envelope lowerhex,
-// delegation:ABC serialized delegation lowerhex}. Native defaults remain
-// unchanged: minimum stake1e12, dust1e10, maturity2016,8 inventory neighbors,
-// confidence128. Public proofs are persisted under the isolated node namespace;
-// session keys and delegation credentials are never saved to the peer store.
-// IBD is true on authority/recovery loss, pending headers/download/candidate
-// work, height below the explicit minimum, future tip, or tip older than the
-// explicit age. Thresholds do not manufacture peer/quorum/finality evidence.
-// status.avalanche reports actual driver readiness/quorum and tip finality.
-// Enabling/disabling Avalanche changes the storage policy profile; an existing
-// home with different options is refused. Import historical blocks into a new
-// isolated home explicitly. Bounded candidate pages (16 rows/call) enroll valid
-// parked and inactive retained blocks; vote capacity retains the current row
-// while transport/poll Tick continues. No automatic unpark policy is enabled.
-// stdout<=8MiB, nonblocking; output saturation terminates cleanly rather than
-// stalling peers.
-//
-// JSONL requests require id:string1..64 and command. status/stop take no
-// extras; submitblock adds block:lowerhex; coin/proof add
-// txid:64lowerhex,index:u32; blockstatus adds block_id:64lowerhex. Responses
-// echo id and ok. Retention is never acceptance: submitblock returns
-// pending_validation; blockstatus reports durable invalid_root, historical
-// ever_connected and authoritative is_active_tip. blockstatus additionally
-// binds block_id and reports block_observation:{observation_available,reason}
-// where reason is available|disabled|unavailable. Only available observations
-// include known,valid,active,parked,finalized,conflicting_finalized,forks_active,
-// has_data, copied from the requested block's native policy observation.
-// Unavailable includes bounded error; disabled/unavailable omit block flags.
-// ready/tip events and status report authoritative metadata and peer counters. EOF exits; no
-// signing/transaction relay, wallet secrets or mainnet initialization.
-// Additional exact commands:
-// mineblock requires id,command,expected_parent:64lowerhex,time:JSONu48,
-// max_claim:canonical decimalu64 STRING,coinbase_output:canonical native
-// spendable Output lowerhex/value0,coinbase_data:null|nonemptyhex<=8192bytes,
-// transactions:ordered full signed canonical transaction hex[] (<=65535),
-// start_nonce:canonical decimalu64 STRING,max_attempts:JSONinteger0..256.
-// Aggregate decoded transaction/destination/data bytes are preflight-bounded
-// by manifest bodycap before copies; the builder separately caps full wire.
-// At most one mineblock executes per loop turn. No cache, mempool or keys.
-// Abort-only Runtime::BuildTemplate and bounded nonwrapping nonce search never
-// establish acceptance. Exhaustion returns found:false,next_nonce:string|null
-// with no admission; found returns coinbase_txid,coinbase_index0,coinbase_value
-// and nonce as decimal strings plus the existing pending-retention fields.
-// Build/resource/deferred/stale failures are typed operational results, never
-// deterministic invalidity facts. Found admission can store a header before a
-// later retention failure; no atomic rollback is promised.
-// readblock requires id,command,block_id:64lowerhex,offset:JSONu32,
-// length:JSONinteger1..65536. Only previously connected disk bodies are served,
-// never pool-only candidates. Return block_id,offset,total_bytes,data:lowerhex,
-// eof and authoritative status. Offset==size is empty/eof; offset>size rejects.
-// Each query may read/copy the whole body within manifest bodycap; returned
-// chunk is <=64KiB. These are logical byte/work bounds, not RSS claims.
-// walletcontext exact request<=1024B:{id,command,tip:null|64lowerhex,
-// outpoint:null|{txid:64lowerhex,index:JSONu32}}. Refuses recovery/receipt/
-// propagation/reopen/paused authority. Optional tip mismatch is stale.
-// Exact success<=32768B:{id,ok:true,chain_id,genesis_id,profile_digest,tip,
-// height,utxo_root,state_root,monetary_bytes,tip_header,history,proof}.
-// History is exactly min(height+1,11) raw134B headers newest-first including
-// tip. Proof is null for snapshot, otherwise the existing coin proof object.
-// Exact failures:{id,ok:false,result:stale|inconclusive|storage_error|invalid,
-// error<=1024B}. Single-owner readonly query binds header/state/proof and
-// rechecks authoritative tip/root/profile before publication. This is a local
-// authenticated snapshot, not a full-chain proof or trust/profile adoption.
-// Storage metadata snapshots retain their separate creation-cap copy bounds;
-// the32KiB returned response bound is not an RSS or backend-read claim.
-int RunDevelopmentNodeCommand(int argc, char *argv[]);
-} // namespace lotus::v2
-#endif
