-# Initial download completion latch
-
-The node retains its existing height, tip age, future-tip and synchronization
-checks until the first successful catchup observation. Completion then latches
-for that Node instance, matching pinned ABC's `IsInitialBlockDownload` process
-latch. Routine header refresh, download jobs, candidate choices and later tip
-aging do not re-enter initial download. Constructing a fresh Node resets the
-latch. No minimum height, maximum age or Avalanche voting default changes.
-
-This catchup flag does not grant current chain authority. The driver's separate
-Snapshot/Tick/Status checks still refuse pending journal, receipt, propagation,
-reopen or paused states and fence the current tip and context generation.
-
-`initial_download_test` extracts the exact production method and latch member
-from `development_node_command.cpp`. Boundary fixtures exercise all original
-startup conditions, first completion, subsequent synchronization noise, aging,
-authority loss and a fresh instance. Optional `initial_download_authority_test`
-links the actual native runtime and Avalanche driver. After completed catchup it
-creates a real native pending journal, checks Tick returns NotReady before
-polling, and confirms current quorum readiness remains false while IBD stays
-false. The native fixture is an observer and does not claim funded quorum
-establishment or finalized polling; those remain separate nine-node gates.
-
-```sh
-cmake -S src/lotus_v2/initial_download_test -B build-initial-download-review -G Ninja \
-  -DLOTUS_INITIAL_DOWNLOAD_NATIVE_AUTHORITY=ON \
-  -DLOTUS_ABC_BUILD=/private/tmp/lotus-v2-daemon-runtime-staging-20261015/build \
-  -DLOTUS_SECP_LIBRARY=/private/tmp/lotus-v2-daemon-runtime-staging-20261015/build/src/secp256k1/libsecp256k1.a \
-  -DLOTUS_BOOST_INCLUDE=/opt/homebrew/include
-cmake --build build-initial-download-review \
-  --target initial_download_test initial_download_authority_test -j2
-ctest --test-dir build-initial-download-review \
-  -R '^initial_download(_authority)?_test$' --output-on-failure
-```
-
-Without the native option, only the small dependency-free policy test builds.
