-// One dispatcher per runtime borrows ONE shared manager for all peers. Borrowed
-// transports/runtime/manager must outlive it. Attach before Open; one physical
-// transport is registered once. Destruction closes attached connections and
-// releases their manager state. No sockets, chain Tick or profile defaults.
-// All mutation is single-owner/nonreentrant, including injected callbacks.
-//
-// Manager callbacks are coordinator-owned: recheck immutable indexed header,
-// profile/invalidity and this FetchEpoch, retain full authenticated bytes under
-// the live download lease, and return RetainedAuthenticated rather than
-// Accepted. Runtime selector context_generation is NOT the fetch epoch.
-// Ordinary tip/body/ header changes and planned recovery preserve fetch jobs.
-// Authority loss or invalid_epoch changes cancel; already transport-queued
-// bytes cannot retract. Pending application input/output survives these fences
-// with its original limits/deadlines; authority loss pauses processing until
-// a fresh runtime snapshot is available. Consumers validate current context.
-// The driver separately advances runtime.Tick and
-// schedules choices.best_fetch.
-//
-// Application notices retain at most max_notices * max_payload_bytes bytes;
-// configuration rejects a product exceeding size_t. TakeNotice transfers the
-// payload charge to its caller.
-// Logical byte caps cover retained event, pending output and bounded decoded
-// headers/inventory per peer, plus bounded compact guards/notices. Transport,
-// manager staging, runtime pool residency and serving transient lease remain
-// separately charged. Vector/allocator overhead and backend creation/query caps
-// are not RSS or exact Get-count claims. Tick bounds query CALLS and item
-// counts.
-// The enclosing driver MUST drain TakeNotice before and after every Tick,
-// independently of diagnostic/stdout backpressure. A full notice queue applies
-// application and manager-event backpressure, including timeout processing.
-// Progress/deadline guarantees require pumping Tick with usable transport
-// budgets and consuming notices; no background thread advances these methods.
-class PeerDispatcher {
-public:
-    PeerDispatcher(DevelopmentRuntime &, DownloadManager &, DispatcherConfig,
-                   DispatcherCallbacks);
-    ~PeerDispatcher() noexcept;
-    PeerDispatcher(const PeerDispatcher &) = delete;
-    PeerDispatcher &operator=(const PeerDispatcher &) = delete;
-    DispatcherResult Attach(Transport &, ConnectionId &out);
-    DispatcherResult Open(ConnectionId, uint64_t monotonic_ms);
-    DispatcherResult Remove(ConnectionId);
-    DispatcherResult StartHeaders(ConnectionId, const Hash &stop,
-                                  uint64_t monotonic_ms);
-    DispatcherResult RequestBlock(ConnectionId, const Header &, DownloadMode,
-                                  uint64_t monotonic_ms);
-    DispatcherUsage Tick(uint64_t monotonic_ms, uint64_t wall_seconds,
-                         uint64_t future_window, const DispatcherBudget &);
-    std::optional<DispatcherNotice> TakeNotice();
-    uint64_t FetchEpoch() const;
-    // Coordinator callbacks may read this sample during manager calls. No
-    // header eligibility rule or clock source is duplicated by the dispatcher.
-    std::optional<DispatcherHeaderClock> HeaderClock() const;
-    std::optional<PeerHandle> Handle(ConnectionId) const;
-    std::optional<uint64_t> ActiveFeatures(ConnectionId) const;
-    std::optional<uint32_t> ActiveLimit(ConnectionId) const;
-    std::optional<NegotiatedTranscript> Transcript(ConnectionId) const;
-    // Negotiated Avalanche messages, or tx and type-1 inv/getdata/notfound; requires negotiated relay.
-    // Busy preserves the existing pending output; caller retains its action.
-    DispatcherResult SendApplication(ConnectionId, Message, uint64_t monotonic_ms);
-
-private:
-    struct Impl;
-    std::unique_ptr<Impl> impl_;
-};
-} // namespace lotus::v2::peer
-#endif
